{"title":"2006 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The vertices of a right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> inscribed in a circle divide the circumference into three arcs.\nThe right angle is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, so that the opposite arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is a semicircle while arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> are\nsupplementary. To each of the three arcs, we draw a tangent such that its point of tangency is the\nmidpoint of that portion of the tangent intercepted by the extended lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. More precisely,\nthe point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> on arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of the segment joining the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03ed03dc1fea29ad8c02cc9ea16ef16d85b49e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D^\\prime$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />\nand <span style=\"color:red\">$D^\\prime^\\prime$ (Error compiling LaTeX. Unknown error_msg)</span> where the tangent at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the extended lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Similarly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\nProve that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is equilateral.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the intersection of the tangents at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be labeled <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/c/5bcc9a9f65fe4e8d33fea4d1bae1fabf5a1e36f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z, X,Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />, respectively.\n</p><p>It is a well-known fact that in a right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c587b0c1e5de0bde79b9d8c36913c16dee04d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> the midpoint of hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6916b50feec24773d374eaada26a95bcabc6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/2284e41ea090ad1157b97cb07229d60d99577b06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651915646f0f43ebe131d3165b9a9a4ea0aed4c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> are isosceles.\n</p><p>Now we do some angle-chasing:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5a4c7754206e79874d6a94d6029ae91e8f5bc2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\angle{EDF} &amp;= \\angle{EDA} + \\angle{ADF} \\\\                      &amp;= \\angle{XEA} + \\angle{AFX} \\\\                      &amp;= (180^\\circ - \\angle{AEZ}) + (180^\\circ - \\angle{YFA}) \\\\                      &amp;= 2\\angle{FAB} + 2\\angle{CAE}\\\\                      &amp;= 2(\\angle{FAE} - 90^\\circ)\\\\                      &amp;= 2(90^\\circ - \\angle{EDF}), \\end{align*}\" width=\"354\" height=\"142\" />\nwhence we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/3/39325fb75bcba7ae553381f29e872747e8441343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EDF} = 60^\\circ.$\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Next, we prove that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486fb42f29e4512faba66c145decfcab8f41185f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DYF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is equilateral. To see this, note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b5de4ffd227ce1bd37729ff0c16ca35a9ffb4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\angle{DYF} &amp;= \\angle{FAB} + \\angle{BAD} \\\\                      &amp;= \\angle{FDY} \\\\                      &amp;= \\angle{YFD}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"214\" height=\"63\" />\nHence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/7/e674685375c53f805e8d13d30fe0b5f8ecbbff9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{FED} = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" /> as well, so triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is equilateral as desired.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO\" title=\"2006 Canadian MO\">2006 Canadian MO</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO\" title=\"2006 Canadian MO\">2006 Canadian MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO_Problems\" title=\"2006 Canadian MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last question</b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016231255\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.557 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 221/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 720/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 47/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6813/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.675      1 Template:CanadaMO_box\n100.00%   12.675      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4551:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016231255 and revision id 39070. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}